<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Meiggs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1811–1877</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Meiggs was an American railway builder who, after fleeing debts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> in 1854, built railways in Chile and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. From 1870 he undertook Peru's great railway programme, including the Central Railway from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callao">Callao</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> across the Andes, one of the highest railways in the world, financed with guano-backed loans. He died in Lima in 1877, with the line unfinished after Peru's finances collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-meiggs.jpg" alt="Henry Meiggs" width="320" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archivo Fotográfico de la Universidad de Chile · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_Meiggs_2.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
